diagnostic_evidence.quote:
Replace $T_{11}$ and $\hat{v}_A$  by $A$ and $b$, respectively, 
together with Lemma \ref{lem:pro}, we may specify the conditions that matrix $A$ and vector $b$ are satisfied, and rewrite equation \eqref{eq:v2}  as 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:equation1}
Ax-\mu_xx=b,
\end{equation}
where $A=\alpha I_n-T_n(a)\in \mathbb R^{n\times n}$ with $a(z)=\sum_{i=1-n}^{n-1}a_iz^i$ and $\alpha =2-\|a\|_{\w} $ is an invertible $M$-matrix.

failure_location.quote:
Equation \eqref{eq:equation1} has a solution $x$ if and only if   equation \begin{equation}\label{eq:mumu}
    \mu=\|(A-\mu I)^{-1}b\|_1
\end{equation} has a solution $\mu$.
